Modifications: wrapped in a padded viewBox and given an explicit GitHub-ink
fill (#1f2328) so they render correctly as cytoscape badge background-images.
The github-platform icon uses the `mark-github` glyph (the GitHub logo /
mark), used here nominatively to denote the GitHub platform.

github-action.svg is TAP-drawn, not derived from Octicons: GitHub retired the
`github-action` glyph from the set (absent from the icons/ directory at v19.15.1;
inventoried from the directory, not keywords.json, which still lists it). Drawn to
sit with the Octicons family — same 24-unit grid, same #1f2328 ink — with a <title>.

actions-artifact.svg is derived from the Octicons `package` glyph at v19.15.1 — the icon
GitHub itself uses for a run's uploaded artifacts — with the same padded viewBox, explicit
#1f2328 fill and <title> as the rest of the derived set.

git-commit.svg is derived from the Octicons `git-commit` glyph at v19.15.1, with the same
padded viewBox, explicit #1f2328 fill and <title> as the rest of the derived set.

status-check.svg is derived from the Octicons `check-circle` glyph at v19.15.1 — the glyph
GitHub renders beside a passing required check — with the same padded viewBox, explicit
#1f2328 fill and <title> as the rest of the derived set.

code-scanning-alert.svg is derived from the Octicons `codescan` glyph at v19.15.1 — the glyph
GitHub renders beside a code scanning alert — and code-scanning-analysis.svg from the Octicons
`codescan-checkmark` glyph at the same version — the glyph GitHub renders for a completed scan.
Both carry the same padded viewBox, explicit #1f2328 fill and <title> as the rest of the derived
set; the 21-unit glyphs are translated by 1.5 to centre them on the 24-unit grid.

dependabot-alert.svg is derived from the Octicons `dependabot` glyph at v19.15.1 — the glyph
GitHub renders beside Dependabot — with the same viewBox, explicit #1f2328 fill and <title> as the
rest of the derived set; the glyph is already on the 24-unit grid, so it needs no translate.

collection-scope.svg is TAP-drawn, not derived from Octicons: GitHub has no glyph for "what one
credential could see on one run", because GitHub does not model it. A viewfinder — four corner
brackets around an aperture — drawn to sit with the family: same 24-unit grid, same #1f2328 ink,
with a <title>.
